---
title: Eggnog
description: Today we're diving into the creamy, dreamy world of homemade eggnog. That's right, you're about to become a holiday hero, whipping up a batch of eggnog that's so luxuriously rich, it'll have your guests coming back for seconds, thirds, and hey, who's counting? I promise, this is one recipe you're going to love. So, grab your whisk, and let's get cracking—literally—because those fresh eggs are the secret to a truly fantastic eggnog.
image: https://eadn-wc02-12309146.nxedge.io/wp-content/uploads/2021/12/THUMBNAIL-EGGNOG.jpg
source: https://chefjeanpierre.com/recipes/eggnog/
author: Chef Jean-Pierre
---

> TL;DR - eggnog is just an ice cream base with meringue.

Separate @eggs{6} into yolks and whites. 

In a #stand mixer{} beat the egg whites until you don't see any yellow tint. Add @sugar{1/3%cup} and beat until soft peaks form.

Whisk (cream) the yolks in a #bowl with @sugar{1/3%cup}, @cinnamon{1/4%tsp}, @nutmeg{1/4%tsp}, and @cloves{dash}. Add @salt{pinch} and @vanilla extract{1%tbsp}. Continue whisking until just combined.

Warm up @heavy whipping cream{1%cup} and @whole milk{2%cups} to a soft boil in a #pot.

Temper the yolk mixture by adding the hot milk and cream mixture SLOWLY. Continue mixing until all liquid is added.

Return the pot to the stove and cook the mixture until it coats the back of a spoon (about ~{7%minutes}). Be careful to not let it boil, so stir constantly.

Transfer to a clean #bowl.

Incorporate the meringue with the egg yolk mixture. If making alcoholic eggnog, add your @?bourbon{2%oz}(Evan Williams Bottled-in-Bond) and @?rum{2%oz}(Myer's Dark Rum) and mix until combined.

Refrigerate for a few hours, or better yet, overnight. 

Decorate with @?whipped cream{} and @?cinnamon sticks{}.
